    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (72.97) anchor the lineup as our most efficient plays. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive 10% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Bassitt (4.73 xERA), with the optimizer leaning heavily into his dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a core build component; while his base projections are high, he maintains a steady score despite the presence of Lugo on the mound, buoyed by a prime #3 spot in the order. **Cal Raleigh** (70.73) and **Zack Gelof** (66.23) also stand out as \"Strong\" starts; **Cal Raleigh** is uniquely positioned to exploit Scherzer\u2019s vulnerability to power (5.40 xERA), and **Zack Gelof** finds himself in the same high-upside environment as **Lawrence Butler**, allowing him to play well above his standard floor despite a neutral R/R platoon grade.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved the marginal range where **Yainer Diaz** (53.73), **JJ Bleday** (53.80), and **Jonathan Aranda** (55.07) reside. While **Jonathan Aranda**\u2019s score is inflated by a spot in the #2 hole, his -12% platoon penalty against Ray highlights the volatility of this start. **JJ Bleday** narrowly edges out the group due to a robust +14% platoon adjustment, which effectively offset the challenge of facing a high-skill arm in Imanaga. On the bench, **Justin Crawford** was the closest to cracking the lineup; however, his sub-optimal L/L matchup against Kikuchi coupled with his exclusion from the confirmed starting lineup resulted in a forced benching. We continue to monitor the status of **Will Smith** and **Matt Chapman**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, while **Dylan Beavers**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Alex Freeland** are currently not in the daily rotation.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, particularly with **Gleyber Torres** (40.18). His start is strictly a tactical necessity, as he faces a significant downgrade against the elite skill profile of Glasnow (2.87 xERA). While **Gleyber Torres** draws a top-of-the-order boost, his negative skill differential is the most concerning on the sheet today. We have also flagged **Daulton Varsho** (49.18) as a marginal start; while he provides necessary coverage, his efficiency is capped by his placement at #6 and a negative park factor. Ensure all game caps are monitored closely, as the gap between our \"Strong\" tier and the sub-40 floor remains tight heading into the evening games.",
